  "steps": [
    "Pat the salmon fillets dry and season both sides with salt and black pepper.",
    "Whisk the tahini, lemon juice, grated garlic and water in a small bowl until smooth and pourable. Add a little more water if needed.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a non-stick frying pan over medium-high heat. Cook the salmon for 3 to 4 minutes on the first side, until well browned, then turn and cook for another 2 to 4 minutes until just cooked through.",
    "Transfer the salmon to plates and spoon over the tahini lemon sauce.",
    "Scatter the parsley, dill and mint over the top and serve right away."
